  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through next Friday)\nIssued at 1043 PM CDT Fri Sep 4 2026\n\nA large upper trough in the Pacific Northwest will slowly move\nthrough the intermountain west by mid week and gradually flatten \nthe large upper ridge over the central CONUS. This should allow \nslightly cooler temperatures across the region (although it will \nstill be hot). Temperatures will be mainly mid to upper 90s and \nthe favored locations (Borger, Canadian, Boys Ranch) could reach \n100-102). There will be another chance of precipitation by mid \nweek but it is a low chance at this time. Until then above normal \ntemperatures and below normal precipitation can be expected.",
